Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:20:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tui_gateway: LINEAGE_LIMIT is _session_lineage's
 default by construction; lineage docstrings say what they read

Follow-up to PR #2117 review 5889960215 (card t_01a1d4990702ec69), three non-blocking nits:

1. lineage_ledger_status's docstring said "least forwardable status", but sorted(statuses)[0] is the
   alphabetically first one; the forwardable states have no order among themselves. It now says
   "alphabetically first (deterministic)".
2. with_parents walks every id's chain, the gateway's lineage root included, so on a chain deeper than
   LINEAGE_LIMIT the gateway reads a superset of the legacy ids (the root the legacy 8-hop walk from the chat
   stops short of). Documented on with_parents and lineage_ledger_status ("the same lineage up to
   LINEAGE_LIMIT hops") with why that direction is safe: an extra `unknown` row only makes the gateway decline,
   and a forwardable one sits on the root the gateway read before with_parents existed, under the durable
   per-row claim.
3. session_notifications._session_lineage defaults to kanban_leg_custody.LINEAGE_LIMIT instead of a second
   literal 8, so the two walks agree by construction; the inspect.signature parity assert is dropped
   (change-detector shape). The depth test of with_parents stays.

No behavior change (the session_notifications kanban_notice_text imports are regrouped to keep the file at its
2000-line cap). Tests: test_kanban_tui_sibling_custody + test_kanban_tui_owner_delivery +
test_kanban_remote_owner_delivery 69 passed; every test file importing session_notifications,
kanban_leg_custody, kanban_tui_owner or kanban_remote_owner (25 files) 372 passed. scripts/check ok.
